# text = The ironical clinch to his sorrow was given by the thought that the intimacy between his cousin and the schoolmaster had been brought about entirely by himself Jude's old and embittered aunt lay unwell at Marygreen , and on the following Sunday he went to see her -- a visit which was the result of a victorious struggle against his inclination to turn aside to the village of Lumsdon and obtain a miserable interview with his cousin , in which the word nearest his heart could not be spoken , and the sight which had tortured him could not be revealed .
