# text = She described what an odd little maid Sue had been when a pupil at the village school across the green opposite , before her father went to London -- how , when the vicar arranged readings and recitations , she appeared on the platform , the smallest of them all , " in her little white frock , and shoes , and pink sash "; how she recited There was a sound of revelry by night ," and " The Raven "; how during the delivery she would knit her little brows and glare round tragically , and say to the empty air , as if some real creature stood there corroborated the sick woman reluctantly
