# text = At first he felt that this nearness was a distinct reason for not going southward at all ; but Christminster was too sad a place to bear , while the proximity of Shaston to Melchester might afford him the glory of worsting the Enemy in a close engagement , such as was deliberately sought by the priests and virgins of the early Church , who , disdaining an ignominious flight from temptation , became even chamber-partners with impunity .
