# text = He went under the stairs , and produced a bottle of cider-wine , of which they drank a rummer each he continued Gillingham accompanied his friend a mile on his way , and at parting expressed his hope that this consultation , singular as its subject was , would be the renewal of their old comradeship were his last words , flung into the darkness after Phillotson ; from which his friend answered But when Phillotson was alone under the clouds of night , and no sound was audible but that of the purling tributaries of the Stour , he said murmured Gillingham , as he walked back alone .
