# text = The pair , however , were so absorbed in their own situation that their surroundings were little in their consciousness said Sue , without enthusiasm said he with some gloom he expostulated ; yet there was misgiving in his own voice also she sighed Jude fell back upon his old complaint -- that , intimate as they were , he had never once had from her an honest , candid declaration that she loved or could love him he said , with a dubiousness approaching anger Sue , who was regarding the distance , had acquired a guilty look ; and she suddenly replied in a tragic voice After this the subject of marriage was not mentioned by them for several days , though living as they were with only a landing between them it was constantly in their minds .
